# abe-froman environment template — copy to `.env` and fill in
# the keys you actually need. `.env` is gitignored; this file
# (`.env.example`) is committed as the template.
#
# Every assignment below starts with `#` so a fresh `cp .env.example
# .env` produces a file that resolves to "no keys configured" — the
# auto-detector reports a clean RuntimeError instead of treating
# placeholder strings as live keys. Uncomment a line and replace
# the value to enable that backend.
#
# Load via:
#   uv run --env-file .env abe-froman run <config.yaml>
# Or in shell:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# Auto-detect order when `--executor` flag and `settings.executor`
# are both absent: Anthropic key → DeepSeek key → ACP via `npx`.
# Raises `RuntimeError` if none configured.

# --- Anthropic (native AnthropicBackend) ----------------------------
# Used by `--executor anthropic`. Auto-detect picks this first when set.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- DeepSeek (OpenAIBackend with DeepSeek base_url) ----------------
# Used by `--executor deepseek`. Auto-detect picks this second.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible providers ---------------------------
# Used by `--executor openai`. Set OPENAI_API_KEY to the provider's
# key and OPENAI_BASE_URL to its endpoint. Examples:
#   OpenRouter:   OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Ollama:       OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   LM Studio:    OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
#   LiteLLM:      OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
# OpenAI's default endpoint is used when OPENAI_BASE_URL is unset.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# --- Resolution order ------------------------------------------------
# 1. workflow YAML setting (when a binding for a particular key exists)
# 2. process env (`os.environ`) — set by your shell or `uv run --env-file`
# 3. this `.env` file, auto-discovered by walking up from CWD
# abe-froman does NOT read from machine-global keystores.
